  "title": "Erdős Problem #688",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Define $\\epsilon_n$ to be maximal such that there exists some choice of congruence class $a_p$ for all primes $n^{\\epsilon_n}<p\\leq n$ such that every integer in $[1,n]$ satisfies at least one of the congruences $\\equiv a_p\\pmod{p}$.\nEstimate $\\epsilon_n$ - in particular is it true that $\\epsilon_n=o(1)$?",
